I smell fresh bread.
I find a bakery stall.
A large chalkboard stands there.
The prices for all the baked goods are on the chalkboard.
I look at the board.
One bread roll costs fifty cents.
One loaf of bread costs four euros.
I step up to the counter.
"I would like four bread rolls, please," I say.
The trader packs the bread rolls into a bag.
"That makes two euros, please," he says.
I look in my wallet.
I find exactly two euros in small coins.
I give the trader the money.
He takes the coins.
"Thank you very much and have a nice weekend," he says.
"Thank you, you too," I answer.
I put the bread rolls into my bag.
